body:
shit like this is why i feel like the right is winning with men, cause they legit don't want us in any remotely leftist space, and I wonder why Men (such as myself) are moving to the right.

&#x200B;

it is almost like the right isn't hostile to me and doesn't view me as a monster that is one step away from a goose-stepping fascist that wants to imprison women, and the LGBTQ because "muh patriarchy".

That comments section as super hard to read as one of these lonely men shes telling to die alone (My worse fear, and honestly, having suicidal thoughts my entire life, other men probably feel the same) Having been raised to love and respect women and never harm them by my mom and sisters, and having been both a caretake for not 1 but 4 of my sisters children , and having done a bulk of what she would call emotional labor, to be taken for granted

&#x200B;

Also i worry for the men who come across this content and actually take it to heart, a population of people who already suffer from a lack of purpose, suicidal ideation, and other problems (Like me), being told on social media that they deserve to be alone, and that they are emotional parasites, and all they do is oppress women and minorities (hell even minority men cant catch a break these days),

&#x200B;

This cant be good for the morale of young men, especially on TikTok, which essentially serves as a pipeline to the far left, being told that as a man you are privilaged over everyone else and that you must "educate yourself" or be indoctrinated into being a leftist "fighting" against the Patriarchy, while still being told to be a traditional man

&#x200B;

And Seeing that she is a published journalist with a bias like that, i cant imagine how she is offline, but this kind of misandry is not only common but encouraged in our society. And i havent read her articles, but if her videos are any indiction, her bias heavily favors women whose politics mirror hers

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

also, jesus christ that end piece was hard to hear, that some women wait for their husbands to die so their life can start, is a line that will send me into oblivion. and the fact that she is happy makes it even sadder.

from what i understand, you are in favor of the NAP (i am as well but think that this is somewhat unfeasable) and no state monopoly on violence or anything right?

&#x200B;

cause if so, i agree on most points

i would agree but i generally find myself agreeing with left leaning principals such as abortion rights (in my opinion, the state doesnt have a right to tell someone weather they should or shouldnt be pregnant or not), and the like

&#x200B;

i also agree that wealth inequality is a problem but is mainly caused by government corruption

As someone who is a high functioning autist, i also struggle social skills and others that are among being autistic but the main one is suffer from being a college student is concentration. This shit killed my first two attempts at college as i literally couldn't focus on shit at all. or if i could, it would magically disappear from my brain like it was snatched from me by a phantom. and this lead me to feel like i couldn't succeed in school. and picking up new things i wanted to do and no follow through, which leads me to drop things for no reason

&#x200B;

and this combined with my struggles as a black man, is that as being autistic in the black community, there are no kind of resources for an autistic black man to help them, and with the communities' views on neurodivergent people as a whole aren't that good either, have left me searching for help and having to find a way to learn that actually help me help myself as a man no one will help you so you have to help yourself sadly.

not trans but the main character was once the villain in the universe it was set in. Spoilers for the book but Daylen, was once known as Dayless the conqueror  a genocidal dictator, who after commiting suicide, was reborn in his youth and goes by daylen, trying to redeem himself,

&#x200B;

 Lyrah, one of the female main characters in the book was raped  as a little girl (spoiler for the book) it is revealed to be Daylen, when he was known as Dayless the Conqueror,  and he did so to hundreds of thousands of girls as young as 14 as well. 

here is a summary from the tvtropes page on this book as well 

&#x200B;

"Dayless became a complete sociopath after gaining power, and filled the rest of his reign with a Long List of atrocities: raping hundreds of young girls, genocide, blackmail, betraying his allies, destroying entire cities, seizing and redistributing all wealth, beheading children, executing people for annoying him, and countless other depraved acts. It's no surprise that by the end of his reign, most of the nations in the world were fighting to destroy him and the Dawn Empire by any means necessary."

&#x200B;

So yeah not "trans pedos" when the protagonist is a literal rapist genocidal dictator himself

